From c1ab871772e161b467e9b95769bbe9b5c1aff989 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:30:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Expose passive bounded Avalanche polling and lifecycle
 diagnostics

The authenticated nine-node quorum still misses the finality deadline, and existing status cannot distinguish expired queries, rejected applications and transport closures. Add fixed-size saturating counters, live query gauges and optional current-tip confidence without feeding diagnostics into voting or connection decisions.

Keep response-handler outcomes distinct from application rejection categories and record one explicit cause per tracked connection removal. Unknown causes remain unknown. Focused poll, peer and driver tests and independent review pass; node serialization and a new real quorum run remain separate gates.
